== the as-of, which the tick passes so its own work is not the outage it reports ==
-- two intervals exactly: the threshold is >=, so this reports --
{"present":true,"marker":"2026-09-12T10:00:00+01:00","gap_seconds":120,"had_lane":true,"report":true}
-- one second short of it: it does not --
{"present":true,"marker":"2026-09-12T10:00:00+01:00","gap_seconds":119,"had_lane":true,"report":false}
-- an as-of before the marker, which a clock set backwards would give: no outage to report --
{"present":true,"marker":"2026-09-12T10:00:00+01:00","gap_seconds":-60,"had_lane":true,"report":false}
-- an empty as-of is an absent one, which is how gap_check forwards a caller that passed none --
{"present":true,"marker":"2026-09-12T10:00:00+01:00","gap_seconds":7200,"had_lane":true,"report":true}
